---
import ExternalLink from "../components/ExternalLink.astro";
import Base from "../layouts/Base.astro";
---

<Base
  title="Support NEMAR"
  description="Find the right place to report a dataset problem, propose a fix, improve the website or CLI, or ask for help with NEMAR."
>
  <div class="support-page">
    <section class="support-hero">
      <div class="container support-hero__inner">
        <div>
          <p class="eyebrow">Help us make the archive better</p>
          <h1>Report the problem where it lives.</h1>
          <p class="lede">
            NEMAR is built in public across dataset repositories, the CLI and backend, the website,
            and the documentation. The fastest support is a specific issue or pull request in the
            repository responsible for the thing you are looking at.
          </p>
          <a class="button button--primary" href="mailto:support@nemar.org">Email support@nemar.org</a>
        </div>
        <div class="support-hero__rule" aria-hidden="true">
          <span>dataset</span>
          <span>platform</span>
          <span>website</span>
          <span>docs</span>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="section">
      <div class="container">
        <div class="section-intro">
          <p class="eyebrow">Choose a route</p>
          <h2>One clear report is better than four vague ones.</h2>
          <p>
            If you are unsure, email us. Otherwise, choose the card that matches the object or
            behavior you want changed.
          </p>
        </div>

        <div class="route-grid">
          <article class="route-card route-card--dataset">
            <p class="route-number">01 · A specific dataset</p>
            <h3>Dataset content, metadata, quality, or citation</h3>
            <p>
              Use the dataset's GitHub repository in <code>nemarDatasets</code>. The repository link
              is available from the dataset detail page. This is the best place to report a wrong
              description, missing file, metadata correction, quality concern, DOI detail, or a
              concrete improvement to that dataset.
            </p>
            <p class="route-action"><a href="/discover">Find the dataset →</a></p>
          </article>

          <article class="route-card route-card--platform">
            <p class="route-number">02 · The platform</p>
            <h3>CLI, API, backend, upload, versioning, or conversion</h3>
            <p>
              Open an issue or pull request in <ExternalLink href="https://github.com/nemarOrg/nemar-cli/issues">nemarOrg/nemar-cli</ExternalLink> for systematic behavior: a command that fails, an API contract, authentication, a
              publication workflow, DOI/versioning, or a Zarr conversion problem that affects more
              than one dataset.
            </p>
            <p class="route-action"><ExternalLink href="https://github.com/nemarOrg/nemar-cli">Open the CLI and backend repository →</ExternalLink></p>
          </article>

          <article class="route-card route-card--website">
            <p class="route-number">03 · This website</p>
            <h3>Browser behavior, layout, routing, or sign-in</h3>
            <p>
              Use <ExternalLink href="https://github.com/nemarOrg/website/issues">nemarOrg/website</ExternalLink> for a broken page, confusing interaction, visual regression, redirect, account surface, or a browser-only problem. A pull request is welcome when you can propose the fix.
            </p>
            <p class="route-action"><ExternalLink href="https://github.com/nemarOrg/website">Open the website repository →</ExternalLink></p>
          </article>

          <article class="route-card route-card--docs">
            <p class="route-number">04 · Documentation</p>
            <h3>Missing, unclear, or incorrect guidance</h3>
            <p>
              Use <ExternalLink href="https://github.com/nemarOrg/docs/issues">nemarOrg/docs</ExternalLink> when a page is hard to follow, a link is broken, a command needs an example, or the platform contract needs explanation. Documentation issues improve the path for every future contributor.
            </p>
            <p class="route-action"><ExternalLink href="https://github.com/nemarOrg/docs">Open the docs repository →</ExternalLink></p>
          </article>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="section section--tint">
      <div class="container narrow">
        <div class="section-intro">
          <p class="eyebrow">Issue or pull request?</p>
          <h2>Both are useful; they do different jobs.</h2>
        </div>
        <div class="explain-grid">
          <article class="explain-card">
            <h3>Open an issue when…</h3>
            <ul>
              <li>you found a problem and want the maintainers to investigate;</li>
              <li>you have an improvement idea but not a finished implementation;</li>
              <li>the impact or correct solution still needs discussion.</li>
            </ul>
          </article>
          <article class="explain-card">
            <h3>Open a pull request when…</h3>
            <ul>
              <li>you can make a small, reviewable change yourself;</li>
              <li>you are correcting documentation or a reproducible website issue;</li>
              <li>the dataset owner or platform maintainer can review the proposed fix.</li>
            </ul>
          </article>
        </div>
        <p class="callout">
          For dataset-specific changes, use the dataset repository even when the website is where
          you noticed the problem. That keeps the correction beside the data, its owners, and its
          version history.
        </p>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="section">
      <div class="container narrow report-section">
        <div class="section-intro">
          <p class="eyebrow">Make the report actionable</p>
          <h2>Tell us what happened and what you expected.</h2>
          <p>
            A short, reproducible report helps a maintainer understand whether a problem belongs to
            one dataset, one client, or the platform as a whole.
          </p>
        </div>
        <div class="report-grid">
          <div>
            <h3>Useful details</h3>
            <ul>
              <li>dataset ID, version, or DOI, when relevant;</li>
              <li>page URL, API route, command, or BIDS file path;</li>
              <li>what you expected and what actually happened;</li>
              <li>small reproduction steps and the error message;</li>
              <li>browser, operating system, CLI version, or other relevant environment details;</li>
              <li>a screenshot or log excerpt with sensitive values removed.</li>
            </ul>
          </div>
          <div class="do-not-share">
            <h3>Do not include</h3>
            <ul>
              <li>participant-level data or identifying information;</li>
              <li>access tokens, passwords, private keys, or presigned URLs;</li>
              <li>private data that is not already part of the public issue context.</li>
            </ul>
            <p>
              For privacy, takedown, or other sensitive concerns, start with
              <a href="mailto:support@nemar.org">support@nemar.org</a> and review the
              <ExternalLink href="https://docs.nemar.org/policies/">NEMAR policies</ExternalLink>.
            </p>
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="section section--closing">
      <div class="container closing-card">
        <p class="eyebrow">Still not sure?</p>
        <h2>Send us the context, and we will help route it.</h2>
        <p>
          Email <a href="mailto:support@nemar.org">support@nemar.org</a>. For a public,
          dataset-specific problem, an issue or pull request is usually the fastest route because it
          keeps the discussion attached to the thing being improved.
        </p>
        <div class="closing-actions">
          <a class="button button--primary" href="mailto:support@nemar.org">Contact support</a>
          <a class="button button--secondary" href="/about">Read how NEMAR works</a>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>
  </div>
</Base>

<style>
  .support-page {
    overflow: hidden;
  }

  .support-hero {
    background: linear-gradient(135deg, var(--brand-navy), color-mix(in srgb, var(--brand-purple) 55%, var(--brand-navy)));
    color: var(--color-fg-inverse);
  }

  .support-hero__inner {
    align-items: center;
    display: grid;
    gap: var(--space-12);
    grid-template-columns: minmax(0, 1.2fr) minmax(260px, 0.8fr);
    min-block-size: 480px;
    padding-block: var(--space-16);
  }

  .eyebrow {
    color: var(--brand-teal);
    font-size: var(--fs-xs);
    font-weight: var(--fw-bold);
    letter-spacing: 0.12em;
    line-height: var(--lh-snug);
    margin: 0 0 var(--space-3);
    text-transform: uppercase;
  }

  .support-hero h1 {
    max-inline-size: 12ch;
    margin: 0 0 var(--space-5);
  }

  .lede {
    color: color-mix(in srgb, var(--color-fg-inverse) 82%, transparent);
    font-size: var(--fs-lg);
    line-height: var(--lh-relaxed);
    max-inline-size: 60ch;
    margin: 0 0 var(--space-8);
  }

  .button {
    align-items: center;
    border: 1px solid transparent;
    border-radius: var(--radius-pill);
    display: inline-flex;
    font-weight: var(--fw-semibold);
    justify-content: center;
    min-block-size: 2.75rem;
    padding-inline: var(--space-5);
    text-decoration: none;
  }

  .button--primary {
    background: var(--brand-teal);
    color: var(--brand-navy);
  }

  .button--primary:hover,
  .button--primary:focus-visible {
    background: var(--brand-gold-light);
    color: var(--brand-navy);
  }

  .button--secondary {
    background: transparent;
    border-color: var(--color-border-strong);
    color: var(--color-link);
  }

  .button--secondary:hover,
  .button--secondary:focus-visible {
    background: var(--color-bg);
    border-color: var(--color-link);
  }

  .support-hero .button--primary {
    background: var(--brand-gold-light);
  }

  .support-hero__rule {
    border-inline-start: 1px solid color-mix(in srgb, var(--color-fg-inverse) 30%, transparent);
    display: grid;
    gap: var(--space-4);
    padding-inline-start: var(--space-8);
  }

  .support-hero__rule span {
    border-block-end: 1px solid color-mix(in srgb, var(--color-fg-inverse) 25%, transparent);
    color: color-mix(in srgb, var(--color-fg-inverse) 84%, transparent);
    font-family: var(--font-mono);
    padding-block-end: var(--space-3);
  }

  .support-hero__rule span::before {
    color: var(--brand-teal);
    content: "↳";
    margin-inline-end: var(--space-3);
  }

  .section {
    padding-block: var(--space-20);
  }

  .section--tint {
    background: var(--color-bg-elevated);
  }

  .section--closing {
    padding-block: var(--space-12) var(--space-20);
  }

  .container {
    max-width: var(--max-width-page);
  }

  .narrow {
    max-inline-size: 980px;
  }

  .section-intro {
    max-inline-size: 68ch;
    margin-block-end: var(--space-10);
  }

  .section-intro h2 {
    margin: 0 0 var(--space-4);
  }

  .section-intro p:not(.eyebrow) {
    color: var(--color-fg-muted);
    line-height: var(--lh-relaxed);
    margin: 0;
  }

  .route-grid {
    display: grid;
    gap: var(--space-6);
    grid-template-columns: repeat(2, minmax(0, 1fr));
  }

  .route-card {
    background: var(--color-bg);
    border: 1px solid var(--color-border);
    border-block-start: 4px solid var(--brand-teal);
    border-radius: var(--radius-lg);
    box-shadow: var(--shadow-sm);
    display: flex;
    flex-direction: column;
    min-block-size: 310px;
    padding: var(--space-8);
  }

  .route-card--platform { border-block-start-color: var(--brand-gold); }
  .route-card--website { border-block-start-color: var(--brand-purple); }
  .route-card--docs { border-block-start-color: var(--brand-navy); }

  .route-number {
    color: var(--color-fg-subtle);
    font-family: var(--font-mono);
    font-size: var(--fs-xs);
    margin: 0 0 var(--space-4);
  }

  .route-card h3,
  .explain-card h3,
  .report-grid h3 {
    font-size: var(--fs-xl);
    margin: 0 0 var(--space-3);
  }

  .route-card p:not(.route-number):not(.route-action),
  .explain-card li,
  .report-grid li,
  .report-grid p {
    color: var(--color-fg-muted);
    line-height: var(--lh-relaxed);
  }

  .route-card p:last-child {
    margin-block-end: 0;
  }

  .route-action {
    margin-block: auto 0;
    padding-block-start: var(--space-6);
  }

  .route-action a {
    font-weight: var(--fw-semibold);
  }

  .explain-grid,
  .report-grid {
    display: grid;
    gap: var(--space-6);
    grid-template-columns: repeat(2, minmax(0, 1fr));
  }

  .explain-card {
    background: var(--color-bg);
    border: 1px solid var(--color-border);
    border-radius: var(--radius-lg);
    padding: var(--space-8);
  }

  .explain-card ul,
  .report-grid ul {
    margin: 0;
    padding-inline-start: var(--space-5);
  }

  .explain-card li + li,
  .report-grid li + li {
    margin-block-start: var(--space-3);
  }

  .callout {
    border-inline-start: 4px solid var(--brand-gold);
    color: var(--color-fg-muted);
    line-height: var(--lh-relaxed);
    margin: var(--space-6) 0 0;
    padding: var(--space-4) var(--space-5);
  }

  .report-section {
    padding-block-end: var(--space-4);
  }

  .report-grid > div {
    border-block-start: 3px solid var(--brand-teal);
    padding-block-start: var(--space-5);
  }

  .report-grid .do-not-share {
    border-block-start-color: var(--brand-gold);
  }

  .report-grid li + li {
    margin-block-start: var(--space-3);
  }

  .report-grid p {
    margin-block: var(--space-5) 0;
  }

  .closing-card {
    background: var(--brand-navy);
    border-radius: var(--radius-lg);
    color: var(--color-fg-inverse);
    padding: var(--space-10);
  }

  .closing-card h2 {
    max-inline-size: 22ch;
    margin: 0 0 var(--space-4);
  }

  .closing-card p:not(.eyebrow) {
    color: color-mix(in srgb, var(--color-fg-inverse) 80%, transparent);
    line-height: var(--lh-relaxed);
    max-inline-size: 68ch;
  }

  .closing-card a:not(.button) {
    color: var(--brand-teal);
  }

  .closing-actions {
    display: flex;
    flex-wrap: wrap;
    gap: var(--space-3);
    margin-block-start: var(--space-6);
  }

  @media (max-width: 760px) {
    .support-hero__inner,
    .route-grid,
    .explain-grid,
    .report-grid {
      grid-template-columns: 1fr;
    }

    .support-hero__inner {
      min-block-size: auto;
      padding-block: var(--space-12);
    }

    .support-hero__rule {
      border-inline-start: 0;
      border-block-start: 1px solid color-mix(in srgb, var(--color-fg-inverse) 30%, transparent);
      padding-block-start: var(--space-6);
      padding-inline-start: 0;
    }

    .route-card,
    .explain-card,
    .closing-card {
      padding: var(--space-6);
    }
  }
</style>
